{{Version|4.5}}{{Planetarynav}}
{{icon|district}} '''Districts''' represent large areas of development on a planet dedicated towards a particular purpose. Each world can support up to four district sets: a primary district and three secondary district sets. The primary district can have 2 specializations and the secondary districts can only have 1 specialization each. Each district shows a number of district slots that can be in one of 4 states; built, available, blocked or unavailable. 

The total number of districts that can be built on a planet is limited by the number of district slots, the base number of which is equal to the colony's {{iconify|planet size}}, which may then be modified by [[planetary features]], [[Planetary features#Blockers|blockers]], [[planet modifiers]], or [[traditions]]. Effects of each district set stack with each district built, and contribute to the total district effect. The number of mining, generator, and agriculture district slots is further constrained by the deposit features on the planet. Each district increases {{iconify|empire size}} by a default amount of 0.5.

== Primary districts ==
Each planet has a primary district that can have 2 specializations. The primary district type depends on empire and planet class and will be converted if the world is terraformed or conquered by an empire which uses a different primary district. The number of districts that can be built is limited only by the number of free district slots on the world. The last primary district on the planet cannot be demolished or replaced.
